WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-Have you guys ever noticed

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.467
when you start typing
something on Google,

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:06.467
it automatically tries to
complete the search for you?

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.067
Yeah, it autofills
what you're looking for.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.200
But sometimes their suggestions
are a little off, I think.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.801
I'll show you what I mean.
It's time for Google Autofails.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.167
Here we go.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.133
-♪ Google Autofails ♪

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:18.133
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.434
[ Applause ]

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:21.901
-Look at what I typed in today.
Today I typed in,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:22.901
"How do we come together

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.968
as human beings to prevent..."

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.734
And these three things
popped up.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.234
"...global warming."

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.834
"...the next pandemic."

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.767
..."Golden bachelor in Paradise"

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.100
No, no one wants that.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.200
I don't want to see that.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.133
[ Applause ]

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.367
Here's another one I typed in.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.067
I typed in "Is Taylor Swift
the reason why..."

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.100
And it said,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.734
"...Travis Kelce
is selling more jerseys?"

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.033
"..movie theaters
are making more money?"

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.968
"...Michaels has been out of
beads for the last six months?"

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.834
I go, that's
that's probably why,

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.467
but that's not
what I was typing.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:55.267
[ Applause ]

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.634
After that I typed in,
"I've never seen a bigger,

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.501
